# Trivy does not read comments for logic; these lines are recorded risk
# acceptance for CVEs with no released fix.

# extract-zip@2.0.1 is pulled in only through the dev-only chain
# lighthouse -> puppeteer-core -> @puppeteer/browsers -> extract-zip.
# It unpacks browser archives that @puppeteer/browsers itself downloads
# over HTTPS, in CI and local shells only; nothing in the built site
# depends on it. No fixed version has been published. Remove these
# entries once a patched extract-zip ships and reaches the lockfile.
CVE-2026-19693
CVE-2026-56876

# basic-ftp@5.3.1 is pulled in only through the dev-only chain
# lighthouse -> puppeteer-core -> @puppeteer/browsers -> proxy-agent ->
# get-uri, which declares basic-ftp ^5.0.2. The fix (6.2.1) is a major
# bump outside that range; the FTP client is never exercised - this site
# audits no ftp:// URLs and downloads no proxy scripts. Remove this entry
# once get-uri takes a basic-ftp that includes the fix.
CVE-2026-102990
